<title>UK: Wolsely up amid building sector optimism.</title>
<headline>Wolsely up amid building sector optimism.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Wolseley Plc reached a three-month high on Friday, extending yesterday's sharp gains as the stock was squeezed higher amid signs of an upturn in demand for building materials, traders said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 15p at 479 by 1321 GMT, after reaching a high of 481p -- its highest since mid June.  </p>
<p>Among other building material stocks, RMC Plc was up 16-1/2p at 11.82-1/2 stg, timber supplier Meyer International Plc was up 12-1/2p at 402 and Caradon was up 6-1/2p at 255. -- London newsroom 44 171 542 4366</p>
</text>
